@title INC-2874: duplicate push notifications
@subtitle Peakform Fitness, Messaging team, 2026-09-21. Times in Pacific.
kpi Duplicate notifications | 7,440,000 | over 38 minutes | bad
kpi Recipients | 1,240,000 | meant to get it once | neutral
kpi Opt-outs | 3.4% | 42,160 users, normal 0.2% | bad
kpi App store rating | 4.3 | from 4.6 | bad

## Summary
A weekly workout reminder campaign was meant to go out once to 1,240,000 users. A retry bug in the queue consumer re-sent each message six extra times, so users got the same notification seven times. That made 7,440,000 duplicates over 38 minutes.

## Timeline
- **16:00** Campaign released.
- **16:04** First consumer timeouts begin, and retries start.
- **16:09** Social media complaints appear.
- **16:15** Support pages the Messaging on-call.
- **16:22** On-call pauses the campaign sender.
- **16:38** Queue purged and duplicates stop.

## Contributing factors
The consumer treated a slow downstream acknowledgement as a failure, and it had no idempotency key. The campaign tool allows sends to the entire user base without a staged ramp. The pause switch took 7 minutes to find because it was undocumented.

## Customer impact
Opt-outs from push jumped to 3.4% of recipients, 42,160 users, against a normal 0.2%. The app store rating dropped from 4.6 to 4.3 over the following week.

## Action items
- **Add idempotency keys to the push consumer.** Daniel Okonkwo-Reyes, due 2026-10-09.
- **Require staged ramps of 1, 10 and 100 percent for sends over 100,000 users.** Priya Venkatesan, due 2026-10-23.
- **Document the sender pause switch in the on-call guide.** Messaging on-call, due 2026-09-28.
- **Send an apology notice and in-app note to affected users.** Customer Care, due 2026-09-24.
